## 3. Infrastructure & Architecture Blind Spots + Fixes

> These are not reasons to change the stack. They are **operational pre-conditions** to close in the Hour-1 bootstrap block so they never cost you time later.

### 3.1 Blind Spot → Fix Table

| # | Blind Spot | Failure Mode on Stage | Fix (do this) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **B1** | **CORS preflight** if API is a different origin | Silent `OPTIONS` failure → "Analyze" does nothing on judge's phone | **Same-origin only.** Frontend calls relative paths `/api/audit`. Vercel serves `public/` + `api/` under one domain. No `Access-Control-*` headers needed. |
| **B2** | **Cold starts** on first demo request | 1–3s freeze after judge clicks → looks like a crash | (a) Live Telemetry Stepper (`M3`/`D2`) masks latency with real progress; (b) at **5:45 PM** `curl` every `/api/*` route once to warm containers. |
| **B3** | **Sarvam 429 rate limit** (60 req/min default) | Audio dies mid-sentence during rapid taps | (a) `speechSynthesis` fallback is **mandatory** (already in PRD); (b) stagger Play/Ask clicks by ≥1s; (c) warm TTS at 5:45 PM; (d) handle `429` with a toast + fallback, never a crash. |
| **B4** | **Stateless serverless** silently breaks in-memory state | Local rate-limiter/cache works in `vercel dev`, fails in prod (each invocation = new instance) | **No stateful logic in `api/*`.** Pure stateless proxies. Rate limiting = rely on upstream 429 + fallback. Caching = client-side only (`verifier.js`, `localStorage`). |
| **B5** | **API key exposure** via public env prefixes | `sk-ant-...` visible in browser bundle → instant disqualification + reputational damage | Keys **only** in Vercel env dashboard, read via `process.env.*` inside `api/*.js`. Never `NEXT_PUBLIC_`/`VITE_` prefix. **Gate:** `git grep -E "sk-ant|sk-or-v1"` must be empty before freeze. |
| **B6** | **Payload size** on Vercel (4.5MB body) | Full-res phone photo rejected at edge | Canvas downscale to `max 1500px` color JPEG `0.80` (~200KB) **before** send. Already in `ingest.js`. |
| **B7** | **Provider schema drift** (OpenRouter vs Anthropic) | Works in dev, breaks when you flip env var at event | Single `llm-client.js` normalizes both to OpenAI chat schema + 4-stage `parseJSONFromLLMResponse()`. Test the flip at 3:20 PM. |
| **B8** | **Audio autoplay policy** on iOS/Safari | `bulbul` audio silently blocked on judge's iPhone | First audio must fire from a **user gesture** (the `▶ Play` tap). Never auto-play on load. Fallback toast if `play()` rejects. |

### 3.2 Same-Origin Topology (the one diagram to remember)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph VERCEL["your-app.vercel.app (single origin)"]
        STATIC["/  → static public/ PWA"]
        API["/api/audit, /api/tts, ... → Node functions"]
    end
    BROWSER["Judge's phone / projector browser"] -->|"GET /  (relative)"| STATIC
    BROWSER -->|"POST /api/audit  (relative, no CORS)"| API
    API -->|"server-side keys"| PROVIDERS["OpenRouter (default) → Anthropic / Sarvam"]
```

**Rule:** if you ever type `https://` in a frontend `fetch()`, you have introduced a blind spot. Use relative paths.

