## 4. Agent-Driven Execution Workflow (Claude Code / Kilo Code)

> The failure mode is opening a terminal and typing "build the app." That produces sprawl you debug longer than you'd have written. The fix is **spec-first, then contract-bound parallel modules.**

### 4.1 The 4-Step Loop

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    S1["STEP 1 · Freeze the contracts (before 1:00 PM)<br/>CLAUDE.md · rules/*.json · mock-audit.json · PRD checklist"] --> S2["STEP 2 · Open 3 lanes with file ownership<br/>Backend · Visual UI · Client Engine"]
    S2 --> S3["STEP 3 · First prompt = READ & ACKNOWLEDGE<br/>'Do not write code yet'"]
    S3 --> S4["STEP 4 · Build one module → validate → report<br/>node --test + mock-audit render"]
    S4 -->|"green"| S2
    S4 -->|"red"| S4
    S4 --> AUD["3:20 PM · Fresh-session audit<br/>new agent, paste tree + test output, find drift"]
```

### 4.2 Step 1 — Freeze Contracts First (15 min)

Create these **before** any agent writes code:

| Artifact | Purpose | Who reads it |
|---|---|---|
| `CLAUDE.md` (§15) | Agent constitution: stack, guardrails, file ownership | All lanes |
| `rules/_schema.json` + 4 packs (§11) | Statutory contract the audit prompt must obey | Backend lane |
| `public/presets/mock-audit.json` (§9.5) | Frozen `AuditResult` sample → UI builds without waiting | UI lane |
| PRD checklist (§5) | Feature → validation → pass/fail | You (orchestrator) |

### 4.3 Step 2 — Three Lanes, Explicit File Ownership

| Lane | Owns (write) | Reads only |
|---|---|---|
| **A · Backend & Prompts** | `api/**`, `vercel.json` | `rules/*.json` |
| **B · Visual UI & CSS** | `public/index.html`, `public/manifest.webmanifest`, `public/styles/**`, `public/js/main.js`, `renderer.js`, `negotiate.js`, `vault.js` | `public/presets/mock-audit.json` |
| **C · Client Engine & Safety** | `public/js/ingest.js`, `pii-guard.js`, `prompt-security.js`, `verifier.js`, `audio-sync.js`, `tests/guardrails.test.mjs` | `rules/*.json`, `public/presets/*.json` |

**Two execution patterns:**

- **Pattern A — Shared folder + status files (recommended):** Run 2–3 Claude Code sessions in the *same* folder. Each writes a one-liner to `status/backend.md`, `status/ui.md`, `status/client.md`. Never edit another lane's files. UI never waits for backend — it builds on `mock-audit.json` and flips one constant (`USE_MOCK=false`) when A is green.
- **Pattern B — Kilo Code Agent Manager (worktrees):** Each agent gets its own git worktree. Zero collision risk, cleaner diffs, but you integrate branches at the end. Slower for a solo 4-hour build.

### 4.4 Step 3 — The First Prompt is Not "Build"

Paste this into the first session of **every** lane:

> *"Read `CLAUDE.md` and `rules/_schema.json`. Do not write any code yet. Reply with: (1) your lane's file ownership table, (2) the three non-negotiable security guardrails, (3) the exact command you will run to verify your work before declaring done, (4) confirm the frontend is Zero-build Vanilla ES2020 ESM (not Vite/React/Next), and (5) confirm `LLM_PROVIDER` defaults to `openrouter`."*

Only after it answers correctly:

> *"Now build `[one module]` in `[specific files]`. Validate against `public/presets/mock-audit.json`. Run `node --test tests/guardrails.test.mjs`. Report: files changed, test output, and any assumption you made."*

### 4.5 Step 4 — Closed-Loop Verification (not vibes)

- **Never** accept "I've implemented it" as done. Require: `curl` output for APIs, `node --test` output for logic/safety, and a 390×844 + 1440×900 visual check against `mock-audit.json`.
- **3:20 PM — fresh-session audit:** open a *new* agent session, paste the repo tree + test output, ask: *"Find schema drift, missing guardrails, and anything that violates CLAUDE.md. Do not fix — list."*

### 4.6 Timeboxing Rule

| Clock | Agent posture |
|---|---|
| 1:00–1:25 | You (human) bootstrap repo, paste `CLAUDE.md`, schemas, packs, mock. No agent yet. |
| 1:25–2:05 | 3 lanes build their first module in parallel. |
| 2:05–2:45 | Integration wire-up (flip `USE_MOCK=false`, real `/api`). |
| 2:45–3:20 | Second module pass (negotiator, vault, audio sync). |
| 3:20–4:15 | Fresh-session audit + fix only red tests. **4:15 hard freeze.** |

